EXPERIMENT: 8
Forensic Analysis of evidential image using Pro Discover Tool
Date: 04/03/2026
AIM
Using Pro-Discover Basics do experimental analysis of a Pro-Discover image and
write down an investigation report.
THEORY
The ProDiscover® Family of computer security tools enables systems administrators, consultants,
and investigators find the data they need on a computer disc. Whether you suspect your system has
been hacked or are looking for discoverable evidence in a civil proceeding or criminal investigation,
ProDiscover® will make your job easier, improve your productivity, and preserve the data needed
for any legal proceedings.
FEATURES:
Incident Response: Quickly and positively identify intrusions to your systems without taking your
system down. Get any corrupted system back online quickly and gather the evidence needed to
prosecute an intruder.
Corporate Policy Compliance Investigation: Check for policy violations or conduct internal
investigations remotely through your company's network.
e-Discovery: Improve your productivity and ensure compliance in any civil discovery action.
Quickly search large data sets and find the documents you need. Preserve critical "last accessed"
metadata and document your results.
Computer Forensics: Find all the data, even in hidden HPA sections, Alternate Data Streams, or
Slack space. Create hash signatures for all files and compare them to the information from the
National Drug Intelligence "Hashkeeper" database. Automatically generate reports and
"evidentiary quality" information that will hold up in court.
ALGORITHM:
1. Open ProDiscover and click on New Project. Enter the project number, project name, and
description
2. Select the Capture image option from Action in the toolbar
3. Select the source disk, destination path for saving the data captured, Investigator name, etc, and
then the ProDiscover analyzes the source disk.
4. Select open image and choose the acquired image, click on content view, and select an image.
or click on Action, then Add Image and select the image, then click on Content View and select
image
5. To recover the image, right-click on the deleted file and add the investigator comment, then
right-click and copy the file to a folder.
6. To generate a Report click on view →report
OUTPUT
Result
Experimental analysis of a Pro-Discover image is performed and an investigation
report is generated
